WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.792
KARIM LAKHANI: Whether you're
developing a new product or strategy,

00:00:02.792 --> 00:00:07.110
responding to the changing workforce,
or simply looking for new ideas,

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:11.670
crowdsourcing and open innovation
allow you to find answers and solutions

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.770
in areas you didn't expect.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:17.280
This course presents a foundational
understanding of open innovation,

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.410
helping you not only solve some
of your most difficult problems,

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.460
but also gain access to a
pool of talent that goes

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.090
far beyond your organization's walls.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.690
Through videos, real world case
studies, and peer interaction,

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:34.560
you will explore when and why
to implement crowdsourcing,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.600
how to operationalize
it, and most importantly,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.160
how to identify the problem
you're trying to solve.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.910
JIN PAIK: What we see
with open innovation

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.740
and crowdsourcing is that
as new architecture rises,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.440
to be able to use the
component knowledge to be

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.350
able to access new talent, new
tools, new ways of doing things.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:59.970
LUIS VILLA: Having an open-source
team, open-source strategy as a company

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.930
is very much seen now as a hiring
or recruiting strategy, as well.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.690
LYNN BUQUO: There is a
complete change in attitude

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:11.280
about what the benefit of being
open can bring to the agency.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.060
I see it at all levels
of the agency now.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.050
KARIM LAKHANI: The world is
full of amazing people that

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:23.190
are scattered around the
globe, and open innovation

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.360
allows you to systematically
get access to these people

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.720
and help your company
and your organization

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.940
solve their most difficult challenges.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:37.460
In open innovation, the
world becomes your lab.

